{title: Evening and Morning}
{artist: Paul Gerhardt · tr. Richard Massie}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[F]Evening [Bb]and [F]morning, Sun[Bb]set [C]and [F]dawning, Wealth, [Bb]peace, [F]and [Bb]gladness,
[C]Com[F]fort [Bb]in [F]sadness, [Dm7]These are Thy [Bbmaj7]works; [F]all the glory be Thine!
Times without [Dm7]number, [Cmaj7]A[F]wake or in [Am7]slumber, [F]Thine [Dm]eye [C]ob[F]serves [Dm]us,
[Gm]From [Am]danger pre[F]serves us, Causing Thy mer[Am]cy [C]upon [F]us to [Aaug]shine.

Verse 2
[F]Golden [Bb]and [F]glorious, Strong [Bb]and [C]vic[F]torious All [Bb]joy [F]and [Bb]gladness,
[C]Scat[F]te[Bb]ring [F]sadness, [Dm7]Rises the [Bbmaj7]sun [F]with his lifegiving rays;
Still as the [Dm7]dying, [Cmaj7]My [F]members were [Am7]lying, [F]but [Dm]now [C]up[F]spring[Dm]ing,
[Gm]With [Am]joy I am [F]singing, Gazing around [Am]me [C]with won[F]der and [Aaug]praise.

Verse 3
[F]Mine eye [Bb]sur[F]veyeth What [Bb]God [C]dis[F]playeth Of [Bb]His [F]great [Bb]glory
[C]Spread [F]out [Bb]be[F]fore me, [Dm7]Teaching how [Bbmaj7]great [F]are His wisdom and might;
To His saints [Dm7]showing [Cmaj7]The [F]home where they're [Am7]going, [F]Peace[Dm]ful[C]ly [F]quit[Dm]ting
[Gm]When [Am]God sees it [F]fitting, Earth's closing scenes, [Am]as [C]they fade [F]from their [Aaug]sight.

Verse 4
[F]Let us [Bb]all [F]singing, And [Bb]to [C]God [F]bringing Our [Bb]choi[F]cest [Bb]treasure,
[C]To [F]do [Bb]Him [F]pleasure, [Dm7]Offer a [Bbmaj7]sac[F]rifice sweeter than lambs.
Heartfelt con[Dm7]trition, [Cmaj7]And [F]cheerful sub[Am7]mission, [F]Songs [Dm]of [C]thanks[F]gi[Dm]ving,
[Gm]And [Am]fruits of good [F]living Please Him far bet[Am]ter [C]than in[F]cense of [Aaug]rams.

Verse 5
[F]All here [Bb]is [F]dying, Groa[Bb]ning [C]and [F]sighing; God [Bb]does [F]not [Bb]alter,
[C]Nor [F]His [Bb]Word [F]falter; [Dm7]Built like His [Bbmaj7]will, [F]on immutable ground,
His love re[Dm7]maineth, [Cmaj7]His [F]grace never [Am7]waneth, [F]Soo[Dm]thing [C]and [F]hea[Dm]ling
[Gm]The [Am]pains we are [F]feeling, Keeping us now [Am]and [C]eter[F]nally [Aaug]sound.
